       openssl-env - OpenSSL environment variables

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The OpenSSL libraries use environment variables to override the
       compiled‐in default paths for various data.  To avoid security risks,
       the environment is usually not consulted when the executable is set‐
       user‐ID or set‐group‐ID.

       CCTTLLOOGG__FFIILLEE
           Specifies  the  path  to  a certificate transparency log list.  See
           CCTTLLOOGG__SSTTOORREE__nneeww(3).

       OOPPEENNSSSSLL
           Specifies the path to the ooppeennssssll executable. Used  by  the  rreehhaasshh
           script (see "Script Configuration" in ooppeennssssll--rreehhaasshh(1)) and by the
           CCAA..ppll script (see "NOTES" in CCAA..ppll(1)

       OOPPEENNSSSSLL__CCOONNFF, OOPPEENNSSSSLL__CCOONNFF__IINNCCLLUUDDEE
           Specifies  the  path  to a configuration file and the directory for
           included files.  See ccoonnffiigg(5).

       OOPPEENNSSSSLL__CCOONNFFIIGG
           Specifies a configuration option and filename for the  rreeqq  and  ccaa
           commands invoked by the CCAA..ppll script.  See CCAA..ppll(1).

       OOPPEENNSSSSLL__EENNGGIINNEESS
           Specifies the directory from which dynamic engines are loaded.  See
           ooppeennssssll--eennggiinnee(1).

       OOPPEENNSSSSLL__MMAALLLLOOCC__FFDD, OOPPEENNSSSSLL__MMAALLLLOOCC__FFAAIILLUURREESS
           If  built  with  debugging,  this allows memory allocation to fail.
           See OOPPEENNSSSSLL__mmaalllloocc(3).

       OOPPEENNSSSSLL__MMOODDUULLEESS
           Specifies the directory  from  which  cryptographic  providers  are
           loaded.   Equivalently,  the  generic  --pprroovviiddeerr--ppaatthh  command‐line
           option may be used.

       OOPPEENNSSSSLL__WWIINN3322__UUTTFF88
           If set, then UUII__OOppeennSSSSLL(3) returns UTF-8  encoded  strings,  rather
           than  ones  encoded  in  the  current code page, and the ooppeennssssll(1)
           program  also  transcodes  the  command‐line  parameters  from  the
           current  code  page  to  UTF-8.   This environment variable is only
           checked on Microsoft Windows platforms.

       RRAANNDDFFIILLEE
           The state file for the random number generator.  This should not be
           needed in normal use.  See RRAANNDD__llooaadd__ffiillee(3).

       SSSSLL__CCEERRTT__DDIIRR, SSSSLL__CCEERRTT__FFIILLEE
           Specify the default directory or file containing  CA  certificates.
           See SSSSLL__CCTTXX__llooaadd__vveerriiffyy__llooccaattiioonnss(3).

       TTSSGGEETT
           Additional arguments for the ttssggeett(1) command.

       OOPPEENNSSSSLL__iiaa3322ccaapp, OOPPEENNSSSSLL__ssppaarrccvv99ccaapp, OOPPEENNSSSSLL__ppppccccaapp, OOPPEENNSSSSLL__aarrmmccaapp,
       OOPPEENNSSSSLL__ss339900xxccaapp
           OpenSSL  supports  a  number of different algorithm implementations
           for various machines and, by default, it determines  which  to  use
           based  on  the processor capabilities and run time feature enquiry.
           These environment variables can be used to exert more control  over
           this      selection      process.       See     OOPPEENNSSSSLL__iiaa3322ccaapp(3),
           OOPPEENNSSSSLL__ss339900xxccaapp(3).

       NNOO__PPRROOXXYY, HHTTTTPPSS__PPRROOXXYY, HHTTTTPP__PPRROOXXYY
